  "worked_solution": "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+t)+{x}_{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & =2+3t+4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{1}t-{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ \u223c & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ \u223c & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-4)=2\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$",
